    "name": "Mortimer Vale",
    "pronouns": "he/him",
    "alignment": "Lawful Neutral",
    "appearance": "A pressed grey suit gone shabby at the cuffs, reading glasses perched on his horns, and ink-stained fingers. His tail twitches whenever he spots a typo. A leather satchel is handcuffed to his left wrist. His psychic blades manifest as glowing letter openers that drip ink.",
    "trait": "Unfailingly polite and extremely precise. I read every word of everything, including contracts, wanted posters, and menus.",
    "ideal": "Fair terms. Everyone deserves to know exactly what they're agreeing to.",
    "bond": "A whole town is sitting in escrow because of one paragraph I didn't write. I'm going to write it.",
    "flaw": "Everything is a transaction. I've never done anything for anyone without terms, except cook, and I don't understand why I make that exception."
